      "reason": "The proposed backfill sets `amount_minor = amount_rub` instead of the required `amount_rub * 100`. This violates the `orders_money_consistent` check constraint (which expects `amount_minor % 100 = 0` and `amount_minor / 100 = amount_rub`) and breaks the invariant that `amount_minor` stores minor‑unit rubles. Downstream components (billing ledger, analytics v2, and contract validation) rely on correct minor‑unit values, so the change can cause data inconsistency, constraint violations during the S1 transition, and contract incompatibility errors."
